      "body": "- [x] Analyze current build infrastructure\n- [x] Review existing Python scripts and workflow structure\n- [x] Understand security requirements\n- [x] Create comprehensive implementation plan\n- [x] Develop Python build script (scripts/build_with_logging.py)\n- [x] Develop bundle analysis script (scripts/analyze_webpack_stats.py)\n- [x] Add security validation tests (all passed \u2705)\n- [x] Create comprehensive documentation (7 documents)\n- [x] Update .gitignore\n- [x] Test scripts locally\n- [x] Validate security measures\n- [x] **\u2705 APPROVED BY @litlfred** - Implementation complete\n- [x] Create workflow event logging script (log_workflow_event.py)\n- [x] Modify GitHub workflow to use Python build scripts\n- [x] Add event metadata logging at workflow start\n- [x] Add build artifacts upload with 90-day retention\n- [x] Update PR comments to include build artifacts information\n- [x] Add separate log file for each workflow step\n- [x] Display build artifacts summary in workflow output\n- [x] Create implementation summary document\n- [x] Reply to @litlfred comments confirming implementation\n- [x] Fix artifacts to upload individually (not as single zip)\n- [x] Update PR comment links to show individual artifacts\n- [x] Upload event metadata immediately and provide link at workflow start\n- [x] Show persistent artifact tracking table across all PR comment stages\n- [x] Add artifact URL retrieval and direct linking (e.g., /artifacts/4354118946)\n- [x] Replace artifact status icons with circle buttons (\ud83d\udfe2/\ud83d\udfe1) for consistency\n- [x] Change build-logs to purple circle (\ud83d\udfe3) for distinction\n- [x] Fix artifact links to use actual artifact IDs (not just #artifacts anchor)\n- [x] Add build verification script (scripts/verify-ghpages-build.sh) for reusable build validation\n- [x] Create Copilot instructions (docs/COPILOT_INSTRUCTIONS.md) for agent build verification\n- [x] Fix workflow event logging failures with robust error handling\n- [x] Fix artifact links to use correct direct artifact URLs with artifact IDs\n- [x] Address PR review feedback (event status logic, explicit bash shell)\n- [x] Fix artifact URLs to use browser-friendly format (not API URLs requiring auth)\n- [x] Change build-logs back to green and add verbose npm logging\n- [x] Fix bash syntax error in workflow event logging (use env vars instead of inline JSON)\n- [ ] \u23f3 Test implementation in PR workflow (in progress)\n- [ ] Update README.md and TROUBLESHOOTING.md\n- [ ] Verify artifacts and validate logs\n- [ ] Final review\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Latest Update - Fixed Workflow Event Logging Syntax Error\n\n**Commit**: Fix workflow event logging bash syntax error by using environment variables\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 Changes Made\n\n**Bash Syntax Error Fixed** \u2705\n- Changed JSON passing from inline script arguments to environment variables\n- Prevents bash from interpreting special characters in JSON (like `<`, `>`, `&`)\n- Uses `GITHUB_EVENT_JSON` and `GITHUB_CONTEXT_JSON` environment variables\n- Removed problematic `--event-json` and `--github-json` inline arguments\n\n### \ud83d\udcca Root Cause Analysis\n\n**Problem:**\n```bash\npython3 scripts/log_workflow_event.py \\\n  --event-json '${{ toJSON(github.event) }}'  # JSON with < character causes syntax error\n```\n\n**Error:**\n```\n/home/runner/work/_temp/xyz.sh: line 246: syntax error near unexpected token `<'\nProcess completed with exit code 2\n```\n\n**Solution:**\n```yaml\nenv:\n  GITHUB_EVENT_JSON: ${{ toJSON(github.event) }}  # JSON safely in env var\n  GITHUB_CONTEXT_JSON: ${{ toJSON(github) }}\nrun: |\n  python3 scripts/log_workflow_event.py \\\n    --event-name \"${{ github.event_name }}\" \\\n    --output-file \"artifacts/workflow-event.log\"  # Script reads JSON from env vars\n```\n\n### \ud83c\udfaf Issues Fixed\n\n1. \u2705 **Exit code 2** - Script will now run successfully\n2. \u2705 **Missing workflow-event.log** - File will be created\n3. \u2705 **Workflow-event-log stays Pending** - Will update to Available once uploaded\n4. \u2705 **Bash syntax errors** - JSON special characters no longer cause issues\n\n### \u2705 Benefits\n\n- \u2705 No bash escaping issues with complex JSON\n- \u2705 Works with any JSON content (including HTML, XML, special chars)\n- \u2705 More reliable workflow execution\n- \u2705 Cleaner workflow YAML\n- \u2705 Script already had env var fallback support\n\n**Next**: Workflow will run successfully and create event metadata artifact. \ud83d\ude80\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>Enhance Production Build Workflow to Emit and Archive Detailed Build Logs and Stats</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>@copilot has explicit permission to modify GitHub workflows.\n> \n> the deploy-branch yaml file should be modified to have better logging/debugging capabilities as described below.   we do not need a separate workflow.\n> \n> also as much as possible all GitHub workflows should  stop using J's and bash programming and move things into the scripts/* as python scripts.  I want to protect against github workflow variable injection attacks.  all variables need to be sanitized.  putting all the workflow business logic is  python is more maintainable.\n> \n> \n> DO NOT IMPLEMENT YET - I need to approve a DETAILED implementation and change plan before proceeding.\n> \n> ## Summary\n> Improve the GitHub Actions workflow for production builds so that it:\n> - Emits more verbose/detailed logs (including file-level info and debug output)\n> - Captures full build logs and stats/metafiles\n> - Uploads logs/stats as artifacts for later download and analysis\n> - Documents how to retrieve log files from past workflow runs\n> - Enhances log reporting by using bundler debug flags and generating machine-readable build stats\n> - Uses GitHub Actions artifacts to persist logs and stats for later troubleshooting and analysis\n> \n> ## Proposed Solution\n> - Update the build workflow to tee stdout/stderr to an artifact (e.g., `artifacts/build.log`).\n> - Add steps to generate stats/metafile outputs for webpack, esbuild, or vite (if present).\n> - Upload logs and stats as artifacts using `actions/upload-artifact` so they are accessible from the Actions run page.\n> - Document how to download these artifacts from completed workflow runs for future reference.\n> - Improve log reporting in the build workflow (e.g., show which file is being processed, warnings, errors) by enabling verbose/debug flags for the build tools.\n> \n> ## Key Tips\n> - Use bundler-specific flags to increase verbosity: e.g., `DEBUG=vite:*`, `ESBUILD_LOG_LEVEL=debug`, `npx webpack --profile --json`.\n> - Uploading as artifacts ensures logs persist for the retention period (default: 90 days for public repos, configurable for private).\n> - Artifacts can be downloaded from the \"Summary\" page of any workflow run (navigate to Actions > specific run > Artifacts section).\n> - For long-term retention, consider pushing logs to a dedicated branch or external storage.\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> - Workflow produces and uploads build logs and bundler stats/metafiles.\n> - Documentation is added to the repo (README or workflow comments) on how to access/download log artifacts from past workflow runs.\n> - Optionally, provide a simple analysis step to print largest modules/files in the log for quick inspection.\n> - Improved log reporting in CI/CD build workflow and consistent use of artifacts for troubleshooting.\n> \n> ---\n> **Stored log files can be accessed later by navigating to the GitHub Actions > specific workflow run > Artifacts section. Download the desired log/stat file directly from there.**\n> \n> \n> </issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\nFixes litlfred/sgex#1151\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\u2728 Let Copilot coding agent [set things up for you](https://github.com/litlfred/sgex/issues/new?title=\u2728+Set+up+Copilot+instructions&body=Configure%20instructions%20for%20this%20repository%20as%20documented%20in%20%5BBest%20practices%20for%20Copilot%20coding%20agent%20in%20your%20repository%5D%28https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips%29%2E%0A%0A%3COnboard%20this%20repo%3E&assignees=copilot) \u2014 coding agent works faster and does higher quality work when set up for your repo.\n",
